{:id :EACL-FORMAL-052
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "public-can-map-arity/consistency-false/source-to-model-audit"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 through commit 484e41d913952d41ef329ae2e32c8018e7e0902c"]
 :affected-backends [:datomic :datahike :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "Every backend's public map-form can? used (or consistency :local-snapshot) before descriptor validation. Because false is falsey in Clojure, the malformed explicit value false was silently rewritten to local snapshot even though positional can? and the shared descriptor rejected it."
 :fix
 "Pass the raw map consistency value to the shared descriptor. The descriptor defaults omitted or nil values to :minimize-latency and rejects false as :eacl/unsupported-consistency. Cross-backend regressions cover the public map arity, and Dafny models the public input classes and proves that only omitted, nil, or explicit minimize-latency values normalize to minimize-latency while false is rejected."
 :closing-evidence
 ["ConsistencyDecision.OnlyOmittedOrNilConsistencyDefaultsToMinimizeLatency"
  "ConsistencyDecision.FalseConsistencyCannotSilentlyDefault"
  "ConsistencyDecision.ExplicitConsistencyModeIsPreserved"
